      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "Since right triangles ABC and ABD share angle A, they are similar triangles, thus the ratios of the corresponding sides are equal. The ratio of segment BC to segment AB is equal to the ratio of segment CD to segment AD. Since segment CD is obviously equal to segment AB, and segment AB is equal to 12 since we are in a right triangle with a perimeter of 76 units, we can divide both sides of the equation by 12 to find that segment BD is equal to 1.\nDue to this, if we take the Pythagorean theorem in right triangles ABD and ABD, we can find the length of segment BC to be $\\boxed{15}$ units.",
